== Match report ==

=== Volisania 1–0 Balboa ===
[[Volisania national football team|Volisania]] edged past [[Balboa national football team|Balboa]] in [[Axarquía]] with a late goal in the 84th minute. The match was tightly contested throughout, with both sides creating chances but unable to find the breakthrough until Volisania struck late to seal a place in the quarter-finals.

=== Jarin 0–1 Balisca ===
Co-hosts [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] knocked out [[Jarin national football team|Jarin]] in [[Macaio]] with a late goal in the 85th minute. Jarin had resisted Balisca's pressure for much of the match but were ultimately undone by a single goal.

=== Galwa 0–1 Asikyira ===
[[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] continued their impressive tournament with a 1–0 win over [[Galwa national football team|Galwa]] in [[Valparaíso]]. [[Amadou Baal]] scored the only goal of the match in the 60th minute as Asikyira's tournament top scorer struck again.

=== Hersatia 0–3 Pangkajene ===
[[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] cruised past [[Hersatia national football team|Hersatia]] in [[Telukuba]], with [[Andi Akbar]] (22'), [[Muhammad Asri]] (56'), and [[Daeng Naba]] (88') all finding the net. Pangkajene's attacking prowess proved too much for Hersatia, who were unable to respond.

== Summary ==

The second day of the round of 16 produced 6 goals across 4 matches. [[Volisania national football team|Volisania]], [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]], [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]], and [[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] all advanced to the quarter-finals. All four matches were decided by single-goal margins or clean sheets, with Pangkajene's 3–0 win the most emphatic result of the day.

